        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "f50e993c-6972-32f6-9825-06527149a204",
                "word": "perversement",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "da0c5573-dfcc-371f-81b7-3e48d0a95372",
                        "entry_id": "f50e993c-6972-32f6-9825-06527149a204",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Avec perversité."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d2e96481-bd5b-462f-8b60-c9a110d90ecd",
                                "sense_id": "da0c5573-dfcc-371f-81b7-3e48d0a95372",
                                "text": "Une jeune soubrette dont l'image aguichante s'associa perversement dans mon esprit, à celle d'une aimable fille d'amour, emplit les verres, déposa sur le guéridon deux cendriers, […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "37d1a182-ef14-45e4-b121-956fb5ba51d1",
                                "sense_id": "da0c5573-dfcc-371f-81b7-3e48d0a95372",
                                "text": "Inaccessible au sacré, j’adorais la magie : le cinéma, c’était une apparence suspecte que j’aimais perversement pour ce qui lui manquait encore. Ce ruissellement, c’était tout, ce n’était rien, c’était tout réduit à rien : j’assistais aux délires d’une muraille."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9f92b40d-e47a-45cd-bd40-c6de189dde7f",
                        "source_entry_id": "f50e993c-6972-32f6-9825-06527149a204",
                        "source_sense_id": "da0c5573-dfcc-371f-81b7-3e48d0a95372",
                        "target_lang_word": "perversely",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "perversely",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "985a809d-60ce-3856-b8e2-5598179af6e6",
                                        "entry_id": "3c4c2026-4ef6-397a-a07d-f57549463924",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a perverse manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9be8b57-4c5a-4620-b768-796d31c52800",
                                                "sense_id": "985a809d-60ce-3856-b8e2-5598179af6e6",
                                                "text": "But even if one of the curves is sloped “perversely,” the condition may still be fulfilled […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a418d3b-85c7-41b1-aa49-038ebd03fdec",
                                                "sense_id": "985a809d-60ce-3856-b8e2-5598179af6e6",
                                                "text": "By such perversely exacting standards the possibilities for a genuine, living Inuit art to exist at all are slim."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85993fda-60ae-4581-9e97-c60403457b3b",
                                                "sense_id": "985a809d-60ce-3856-b8e2-5598179af6e6",
                                                "text": "There is another reason the films are so entertaining and successful, though (with the franchise earning more than $500 million dollars so far). Perversely, we love John Wick himself. That lethal, bereaved assassin is a good bad guy for our times, the natural extension of Tony Soprano, Walter White and all the other heroic antiheroes the culture has embraced."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
